%description:
Tests a receive buffer that SO_RCVBUF locked: it counts its memory, not the
bytes of its data, as Linux (tcp_can_ingest()). The server offers 65535 bytes,
and at t=1.001 s, while two 20000-byte segments are on their way, it locks a
buffer of 32000 bytes and does not read. The first segment costs 20712 bytes
of memory, within the buffer, so the second one gets in whole, although its
data end 8000 bytes beyond the buffer; the memory is then over the buffer, and
the next segment would be dropped. The offer keeps the right edge of the
earlier offer, as the window does not move back. Before the repair, the server
also counted the bytes and dropped the second segment.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 40000"
*.srv_app.autoRead=false
*.srv_app.rcvBufScript="1.001 32000"  # SO_RCVBUF: lock a buffer of 32000 bytes before the data arrive
sim-time-limit = 3s
*.*_tcp.mss = 20000
*.*_tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.srv_tcp.advertisedWindow = 65535
*.cli_tcp.initialCwnd = 2
*.srv_tcp.receiveBufferSize = 100000B
*.srv_tcp.windowAutoTuning = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%# the second segment gets in
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.003 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 40001 win 25535 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

